      "title": "Springfield College Careers",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Springfield College Careers Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs | Springfield College Careers page has loaded. Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs | Springfield College Careers page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Springfield College Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Print Apply ﻿ Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Salary $250,000.00 - $265,000.00 Annually Location Springfield, MA Job Type Full-time 12 months 35 hours Job Number 00375 Department Academic Affairs Opening Date 04/25/2026 Description Benefits Description To see the full description of this opportunity, please review the full position prospectus Here (Download PDF reader) . The Provost serves as the College’s chief academic officer and a key member of the President’s senior leadership team. Reporting directly to the President, the Provost provides vision, leadership, and oversight for all academic programs, faculty affairs, and academic operations. This leader will shape the future of Springfield College by aligning academic priorities with market demand, strengthening faculty excellence, and ensuring that the Humanics philosophy continues to differentiate the institution in a rapidly evolving higher education landscape. This is an opportunity for a collaborative, forward-looking leader who can make decisions, move with urgency, and lead through complexity while building trust across the institution. Actual salaries will vary depending on multiple factors, including but not limited to degrees attained, experience, and other considerations permitted by law. Comprehensive compensation details, including any additional benefits, will be communicated upon finalization of the employment offer. Responsibilities • Lead Academic Strategy and Portfolio Alignment: Drive the implementation of the Strategic Plan, ensuring academic programs align with student demand, workforce needs, and institutional priorities. Lead decisions related to program growth, redesign, and sunsetting. • Advance Faculty Excellence and Shared Governance: Strengthen faculty recruitment, development, and evaluation processes. Partner effectively within a shared governance model while ensuring accountability, clarity, and forward movement on key priorities. • Align Academic Affairs with Enrollment and Student Success: Partner closely with enrollment and student success leadership to improve retention, persistence, and outcomes. Ensure that academic programs support the recruitment strategy and deliver strong post-graduate results. • Ensure Financial Sustainability and Resource Alignment: Oversee the academic budget and resource-allocation process. Align investments with strategic priorities and ensure that academic decisions are grounded in financial reality and long-term sustainability. • Strengthen Academic Quality and Accreditation: Ensure academic integrity, continuous program assessment, and compliance with accreditation and regulatory requirements. Lead efforts to maintain relevance and rigor across all programs. • Foster Innovation and Growth: Advance new program development, interdisciplinary initiatives, and partnerships that position Springfield College competitively in health sciences, sport, and wellness. • Build Leadership Capacity: Recruit, develop, and mentor deans and academic leaders. Establish clear expectations and accountability while fostering a collaborative and high-performing leadership culture. • Serve as a Strategic Partner to the President: Act as a trusted advisor and thought partner, contributing to institutional strategy, board engagement, and external positioning. Qualifications Required Qualifications: • Earned terminal degree from an accredited institution • Record of achievement commensurate with appointment at the rank of full professor • Significant and progressively responsible academic leadership experience (e.g., dean, associate provost, or equivalent) • Demonstrated experience supporting faculty development and shared governance • Experience with accreditation processes and academic program oversight • Evidence of excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service Preferred Qualifications: • Experience leading institutional or academic strategic planning efforts • Demonstrated success aligning academic programs with enrollment strategy • Experience managing complex budgets and resource allocation • Record of advancing interdisciplinary initiatives and innovation • Experience supporting online, graduate, or professional education growth • Engagement with community partnerships and workforce development Application Process Applicants should submit: • A letter of interest addressing qualifications and leadership philosophy • A curriculum vitae • A list of five professional references with contact information If you are interested, please email your materials to officeofthepresident@springfield.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities The successful candidate will be a strategic and pragmatic academic leader who is comfortable operating in a complex and evolving environment. They will bring: • Demonstrated success leading academic organizations at scale • A track record of aligning academic programs with enrollment and financial outcomes • Strong fiscal judgment and experience managing academic budgets • Experience leading change, including program development and innovation • A commitment to faculty excellence and effective shared governance • The ability to communicate clearly, build trust, and drive results • A deep appreciation for mission-driven education and student-centered learning The Provost must be both collaborative and decisive, able to engage broadly while advancing the institution with clarity and urgency. At Springfield College we offer competitive and generous benefit options for employees and their families. Tuition benefits for employees and dependents Tuition exchange program for dependents Generous paid time off benefits Paid Sick Leave Benefits 403(b) retirement plan (TIAA) with a generous college match Medical, Dental and Vision plan(s) Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA) Flexible Spending Accounts (health care expenses and dependent care) Life and accident insurance plans Long-term disability Optional voluntary benefits Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Wellness benefits and programs Free use of our state-of-the-art Wellness Center Part-time employees earn pro-rated holiday, vacation and sick leave. To learn more about our Benefit Package, visit our Human Resources page. Employer Springfield College Address 263 Alden Street Springfield, Massachusetts, 01109 Phone 413-748-5678 Website http://www.springfield.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Springfield College Careers Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu Springfield College Careers Job Opportunities Promotional & Transfer Jobs Student Job Opportunities Class Specifications Email Job Alerts Help & Support Translate Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”