s Manager Salary $20.20 - $23.00 Hourly Location Springfield, MA Job Type Full-time 12 months 35 hours Job Number 00388 Department Student Activities and Campus Union Opening Date 07/09/2026 Description Benefits Description Coordinates and maintains Office of Student Engagement account services including, but not limited to maintenance of Student Government Association Accounts for over 50+ recognized student clubs and organizations and office budget accounts. Actual salaries will vary depending on multiple factors, including but not limited to degrees attained, experience, and other considerations permitted by law. Comprehensive compensation details, including any additional benefits, will be communicated upon finalization of the employment offer. Responsibilities - Meet with and assist club members, individually or in groups, with booking flights and hotel rooms for conferences and/or club outings. - Advise and assist clubs with event planning- ie: provide cash boxes, review signage and confirm that the appropriate reservations and authorizations have been acquired. - Work in conjunction with campus offices to process student organization requests- such as Harvest Table food services and SC Print Shop. - Coordinate student organizations’ Transportation Request process including review of paperwork and input of data. - Assist student organizations and advisors with creation of events on event management platforms. - Assist the Assistant Dean of Student & Parent Engagement in making necessary preparations and completing appropriate paperwork to facilitate Office of Student Engagement departmental operations while maintaining confidentiality. This may include the performance of a wide range of administrative duties (i.e. requisitions, assorted documents, contracts, check requests, maintaining files and developing google forms and documents). - Assists in managing an office budget of approx $250,000. - Work with personnel in Accounting and Purchasing offices to keep accurate and up to date financial records-including adding new club information into Banner and Journal Voucher Corrections. - Process deposits through Touchnet software. - Communicate daily with Purchasing Office personnel regarding documents provided for check requests, Costco Card requests, and purchase orders. - Process reimbursements through Emburse Enterprises software. - Assists in managing the student government association budget of approximately $350,000. - Assist Assistant Dean of Student & Parent Engagement with coordination and execution of College-wide events led by the Office of Student Engagement. (Ex. Family Weekend, SOAR, Leadership retreats etc.) - Carry ou t diverse office duties such as processing paperwork, and using a multi-line phone (directing calls to appropriate personnel and answering inquiries). - Oversee office supplies, inventory, and equipment Qualifications - High School Diploma required. - Bachelor's Degree in Business, Education, or related field preferred. - At least 3 years of work-related experience required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Effective keyboarding skills and knowledge of related software including knowledge with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Access, and PowerPoint). Quickbooks, Banner, Touchnet, Google documents and google sheets. Must have excellent grammar skills and telephone etiquette. Excellent customer service skills; or any equivalent combination of training and experience. At Springfield College we offer competitive and generous benefit options for employees and their families. Tuition benefits for employees and dependents Tuition exchange program for dependents Generous paid time off benefits Paid Sick Leave Benefits 403(b) retirement plan (TIAA) with a generous college match Medical, Dental and Vision plan(s) Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA) Flexible Spending Accounts (health care expenses and dependent care) Life and accident insurance plans Long-term disability Optional voluntary benefits Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Wellness benefits and programs Free use of our state-of-the-art Wellness Center Part-time employees earn pro-rated holiday, vacation and sick leave. To learn more about our Benefit Package, visit our Human Resources page. Employer Springfield College Address 263 Alden Street Springfield, Massachusetts, 01109 Phone 413-748-5678 Website http://www.springfield.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards